+# Hitstop decoupling — next-session execution guide
+
+## TL;DR
+
+- PR: https://github.com/KellifizW/2ndFight/pull/44
+- Branch: `arena/01a0589e-2ndfight`
+- Reconnect GitHub, then push the working branch (it is at local commit `efc9ddf`, remote is at `d139573`).
+- There is already a robust hitstop implementation committed locally; it has NOT been verified in CI because GitHub auth expired before the last push.
+- Two patch files are available:
+  - `/home/user/hitstop_pr_full.patch` — full PR diff vs `main`.
+  - `/home/user/hitstop_unpushed_commit.patch` — just the final un-pushed commit (`d139573..efc9ddf`).
+
+## Current state of the repository
+
+- Branch: `arena/01a0589e-2ndfight`
+- Local `HEAD`: `efc9ddf` — `fix: freeze actors before snapshot and restore all players as fallback`
+- Last **pushed** commit: `d139573` — `test: trace hitstop registration inputs`
+- Remote branch is therefore 1 commit behind local.
+- Local working tree is clean (everything is committed).
+- GitHub auth expired during this session:
+  - `git push origin arena/01a0589e-2ndfight` fails with `could not read Username`.
+  - `gh` fails with `HTTP 401: Bad credentials`.
+  - The next agent must reconnect GitHub in Arena before pushing.
+
+## What the feature does
+
+Implements modern decoupled hitstop instead of the old `Engine.time_scale = 0` / `get_tree().paused` approach:
+
+- Only character animation is frozen during hitstop:
+  - `AnimationTree.active = false`
+  - `AnimationPlayer.speed_scale = 0`
+  - `AnimatedSprite2D.speed_scale = 0`, `playing = false`
+- Visual pixel jitter is applied to `Sprite2D` / `AnimatedSprite2D` `offset` / `rotation_degrees`.
+- Background, particles, VFX, projectiles, and UI continue at normal speed (`Engine.time_scale` stays `1.0`).
+- All hitstop parameters are `@export` on `HitStopController`:
+  - `enabled`, `hitstop_frames`, `freeze_attacker`, `freeze_defender`, `freeze_animation_player`, `freeze_animated_sprite`
+  - `jitter_enabled`, `jitter_target`, `jitter_amplitude_x`, `jitter_amplitude_y`, `jitter_rotation_degrees`
+  - `pause_frame_counter`, `debug_log`
+
+## Files changed in this PR vs `main`
+
+```
+scenes/gameplay/world.tscn                              |   7 +
+scripts/combat/handlers/HitResponseHandler.gd          |   5 +-
+scripts/combat/movesets/MoveSet.gd                     |   2 +
+scripts/combat/projectiles/fireball.gd                 |   5 +-
+scripts/core/hit_stop_controller.gd                    | 361 +++
+scripts/core/hit_stop_controller.gd.uid                |   1 +
+scripts/core/player.gd                                 |  19 +-
+scripts/core/slow_mo_controller.gd                     | 110 ++-
+scripts/core/world.gd                                  |   8 +-
+scripts/handlers/AnimationManager.gd                   |   8 +
+tests/frame_tests/cases/test_37_hitstop_decoupled.gd   |  89 ++
+tests/frame_tests/run_tests.gd                         |   1 +
+12 files changed, 565 insertions(+), 51 deletions(-)
+```
+
+## Root cause found so far
+
+Frame tests (GH Actions, Godot 4.7.2 headless) fail only in `test_37_hitstop_decoupled`:
+
+```
+✗ Attacker AnimationTree should be frozen during hitstop, got active=true entries=0 freeze_att=true freeze_def=true
+✗ Defender AnimationTree should be frozen during hitstop, got active=true entries=0
+✗ Attacker AnimationPlayer.speed_scale should also be 0 during hitstop, got 1.0 entries=0
+✗ Defender AnimationPlayer.speed_scale should also be 0 during hitstop, got 1.0 entries=0
+```
+
+The debug counters in the last pushed commit `d139573` showed:
+
+```
+is_active=true remaining=8 hit_slowmo=true begin_ret=true entries_begin=0 active_begin=true
+ctrl_found=true begins=1 finishes=0 cancels=0
+a=DAV d=DEN group=2 reg=4
+```
+
+Interpretation:
+- `begin_hitstop()` IS called, returns `true`, and the controller stays active (`is_active=true`, `remaining=8`).
+- `_attacker` = `DAV`, `_defender` = `DEN` (so participants are valid).
+- Players group contains 2 players.
+- `_register_actor()` is called **4 times** (DAV, DEN, then the all-players fallback twice).
+- Yet `_entries.size()` stays `0` and `AnimationTree.active`/`speed_scale` are never changed.
+- This means `_register_actor()` aborts during its bookkeeping before the freeze assignments took effect. The typed `Array[Dictionary]` member did not persist appended entries in the CI runtime, and because the freeze happened after the snapshot dictionary construction, the abort prevented the freeze too.
+
+## The fix currently committed locally (`efc9ddf`)
+
+In `scripts/core/hit_stop_controller.gd`:
+
+1. `_entries` changed from `Array[Dictionary]` to plain `Array` to avoid typed-array append not persisting.
+2. In `_register_actor()`:
+   - Grab the `AnimationPlayer` / `AnimationTree` / `AnimatedSprite2D` / `Sprite2D` node references.
+   - **Freeze the animation FIRST** (speed_scale = 0, active = false, playing = false).
+   - Only after freezing, snapshot original values and build the entry dictionary.
+   - Even if the snapshot/bookkeeping fails, the character is already frozen.
+3. Added `_restore_all_players_defaults()`.
+   - On `_finish()` and `cancel()`, restore **all** players in the `players` group to normal values before applying per-actor snapshots:
+     - `AnimationPlayer.speed_scale = 1.0`
+     - `AnimationTree.active = true`
+     - `AnimatedSprite2D.speed_scale = 1.0`, `playing = true`
+     - `Sprite2D.offset/position/rotation` to zero
+   - This guarantees restore even if `_entries` is empty.
+
+This makes the freeze and restore behavior resilient even when the dictionary entries do not persist. The visual jitter only runs when entries exist (unchanged), but the frame test does not assert jitter.
+
+## How to apply / push
