+# or view https://github.com/KellifizW/2ndFight/pull/44/checks
+```
+
+Expected: `GDScript static check` pass, `Export Web build` pass, `Frame tests` should now pass the freeze/restore assertions.
+
+## If Frame tests still fail after `efc9ddf`
+
+1. Fetch the CI annotation (public page if `gh` is unavailable):
+   - `https://github.com/KellifizW/2ndFight/actions/runs/<RUN_ID>/job/<JOB_ID>`
+2. The test now reports: `dict=... freezed=... appended=...`.
+   - If `freezed=true` and `dict=true` and `appended=true` but entries still 0 → the `_entries` read is the problem; simplify further (remove `_entries` entirely and use direct actor lists).
+   - If `freezed=false` → the abort is still before the freeze; move the four node-reference `get_node_or_null` lookups into a separate helper and/or remove snapshot locals for any risky property.
+3. If `active=true` persists after `freezed=true`, then some other handler is re-enabling the animation after the hitstop begins. Re-check:
+   - `scripts/core/player.gd` `_physics_process`
+   - `scripts/handlers/AnimationManager.gd` `update_animation_state`
+   - `scripts/core/PushManager.gd`
+   - `scripts/core/world.gd` reset paths
+   - Add `is_hit_slowmo` guard on the re-enabling site.
+
+## Cleanup after CI passes
